<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating the Intersection of Events A and B</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>If \(P[A]={@prob_A@}\) and \(P[B]={@prob_B@}\) and \(P[A\vert B]+P[B \vert A]={@prob_E@}\). Find \(P[A \cap B]\) </p>
<p><b>Note:</b> Give your answer correct to four decimal places or as a fraction.</p>
<p>\(P[A \cap B]=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>\(\displaystyle P[B\vert A]=\frac {P[A \cap B]}{P[A]}\) </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle\qquad \qquad =\frac {P[A \cap B]}{{@prob_A@}}={@1/prob_A@}P[A \cap B]\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle P[A \vert B]=\frac {P[A \cap B]}{P[B]}\) </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \qquad \qquad =\frac {P[A \cap B]}{{@prob_B@}}={@1/prob_B@}P[A \cap B]\)</p>
<p> Thus, \(\displaystyle  \left [{@(1/prob_A)@}+{@(1/prob_B)@} \right ]P[A \cap B]={@prob_E@} \implies P[A \cap B]={@ta@}\)</p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
